  "question": {
    "text": "In the titration of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>KMnO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> and oxalic acid in acidic medium, the change in oxidation number of carbon at the end point is"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "1",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The balanced equation of potassium permanganate and oxalic acid&nbsp; reaction in acidic medium is shown below.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mover><mi>Mn</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mover><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mover><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mover><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mfenced><mrow><mi>dil</mi><mo>.</mo></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mover><msub><mi>nSO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mover><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math></p><p>The initial oxidation state of carbon in the oxalic acid is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math>. The oxidation state of carbon at the end point is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></math>(in carbon dioxide). Hence, the change in oxidation state of carbon at the end point is 1.</p></blockquote>"
  }
